        <description>Scan the main Profit &amp; Loss Account (indirect expenses section, NOT the secondary business account) 
and calculate EBITDA.
Formula: EBITDA = Gross Profit - Total Indirect Operating Expenses, EXCLUDING Interest, 
Depreciation, and Income Tax/Provision for Tax.
Rules:
- EXCLUDE: Bank Interest, Interest on Loans/Overdraft/Term Loan/Car Loan
- EXCLUDE: Depreciation on Fixed Assets
- EXCLUDE: Income Tax / Provision for Tax (if shown)
- INCLUDE all other indirect expenses (salary, rent, travelling, printing, general expenses, bank 
charges, insurance, etc.)
Return only the numeric absolute value (NOT a percentage). If insufficient data, return NA.</description>
